<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tenpa Tsering</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1678–1738</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tenpa Tsering was king of Derge in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kham">Kham</a>, eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tibet">Tibet</a>, in the early 18th century. In 1729 he founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/derge-parkhang">Derge Parkhang</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/printing-press">printing</a> house whose woodblocks for the Kangyur and other Buddhist texts are still in use. Under him Derge extended its territory and became the leading kingdom of Kham.</p></div>
